From 26f5acdf17e3c300d2ed11cb0cc2e5dfbe7fbf68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Rikard=20S=C3=B6derstr=C3=B6m?=
 <Rikard.Soderstrom@permobil.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:07:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rpc: Keep mechanism encoding compatible with protocol
 versions 0 and 1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Commit 6449cfe ("Rework rpc_C_DeriveKey to allow size queries", first
released in 0.25.6) changed how CK_MECHANISM is encoded on the wire:
mechanisms without parameters are no longer followed by an empty byte
array, and mechanisms with parameters gained a leading "has parameter"
byte. The change was applied unconditionally, while the RPC protocol
version range still accepts peers at versions 0 and 1, which use the old
encoding. A server >= 0.25.6 therefore misparses every request carrying
a mechanism from an older client, and an older server misparses them
from a newer client. Calls without a mechanism keep working, so the
failure only shows when signing, encrypting or similar: for C_SignInit
the key handle is read from the wrong offset and the call fails with
CKR_KEY_HANDLE_INVALID (e.g. a 0.24.1 client against a 0.26.x server).

Messages now carry the negotiated protocol version. The client encodes,
and the server decodes, mechanisms with the old format when the
negotiated version is below 2 (p11_rpc_buffer_{add,get}_mechanism_v1),
and with the current format otherwise. p11_kit_remote_serve_module()
passes its negotiated version through the new
p11_rpc_server_handle_version(); p11_rpc_server_handle() keeps using the
maximum version.

Tests cover decoding of a byte-exact version 1 C_SignInit request for
mechanisms with and without parameters, and signing over RPC with both
sides at protocol version 1.

Related: https://github.com/p11-glue/p11-kit/issues/733

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rikard Söderström <Rikard.Soderstrom@permobil.com>
